return {
  ["spell.animate-objects.xphb2024"]={title="Animate Objects",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 240\n\nObjects animate at your command. Choose a number of nonmagical objects within range that aren't being worn or carried, aren't fixed to a surface, and aren't Gargantuan. The maximum number of objects is equal to your spellcasting ability modifier; for this number, a Medium or smaller target counts as one object, a Large target counts as two, and a Huge target counts as three.\n\nEach target animates, sprouts legs, and becomes a Construct that uses the XPHB stat block; this creature is under your control until the spell ends or until it is reduced to 0 XPHB. Each creature you make with this spell is an ally to you and your allies. In combat, it shares your XPHB count and takes its turn immediately after yours.\n\nUntil the spell ends, you can take a XPHB to mentally command any creature you made with this spell if the creature is within 500 feet of you (if you control multiple creatures, you can command any of them at the same time, issuing the same command to each one). If you issue no commands, the creature takes the XPHB action and moves only to avoid harm. When the creature drops to 0 XPHB, it reverts to its object form, and any remaining damage carries over to that form."},
  ["creature.animated-armor.mm2014"]={title="Animated Armor",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 11 | CON 13 | INT 1 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAntimagic Susceptibility\n\nThe armor is incapacitated while in the area of an antimagic field. If targeted by dispel magic, the armor must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against the caster's spell save DC or fall unconscious for 1 minute.\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the armor remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a normal suit of armor.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe armor makes two melee attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-armor.xmm2024"]={title="Animated Armor",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 16\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 11 | CON 13 | INT 1 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe armor makes two Slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-armor-detention-drone.bmt2014"]={title="Animated Armor Detention Drone",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 135\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30"},
  ["creature.animated-ballista.wdmm2014"]={title="Animated Ballista",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 39\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 50 (50d1)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMagic Bolt\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 120 ft., one target. h16 (3d10) fire damage."},
  ["creature.animated-breath.ftd2014"]={title="Animated Breath",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 163\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 15/17\n\nPV: 95 (10d10 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 11 | CON 18 | INT 6 | WIS 10 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Draconic but can't speak\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, restrained, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nChromatic Form\n\nWhen created, the animated breath takes one of five forms, matching its creator's breath weapon: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Poison. This form determines the creature's AC, damage resistance, traits, and attacks.\n\nFire Aura (Fire Form Only)\n\nAt the start of each of the animated breath's turns, each creature within 5 feet of it takes 3 (1d6) fire damage, and flammable objects in the aura that aren't being worn or carried ignite. A creature that touches the animated breath or hits it with a melee attack takes 3 (1d6) fire damage.\n\nPutrid Aura (Acid and Poison Forms Only)\n\nA creature that starts its turn within 5 feet of the animated breath must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned until the start of its next turn. A creature that touches the animated breath or hits it with a melee attack takes 3 (1d6) acid damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe animated breath makes two Slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage plus 11 (2d10) damage of a type determined by the animated breath's form: acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nLightning Burst (Lightning Form Only)\n\nThe animated breath magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 30 feet of it. Each creature within 5 feet of the animated breath after it teleports takes 3 (1d6) lightning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-broom.cm2014"]={title="Animated Broom",subtitle="Criatura - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 17 (5d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 50\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 17 | CON 10 | INT 1 | WIS 5 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Object\n\nIf the broom is motionless at the start of combat, it has advantage on its initiative roll. Moreover, if a creature hasn't observed the broom move or act, that creature must succeed on a 15 Wisdom (Perception) check to discern that the broom is animate.\n\nFlyby\n\nThe broom doesn't provoke opportunity attacks when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe broom makes two melee attacks.\n\nBroomstick\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-broom.xmm2024"]={title="Animated Broom",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 16\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 14 (4d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, fly: 50\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 17 | CON 10 | INT 1 | WIS 5 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe broom doesn't provoke an XPHB when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d4 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-chained-library.cm2014"]={title="Animated Chained Library",subtitle="Criatura - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 45 (6d10 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 8 | CON 14 | INT 1 | WIS 5 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Object\n\nIf the library is motionless at the start of combat, it has advantage on its initiative roll. Moreover, if a creature hasn't observed the library move or act, that creature must succeed on a 15 Wisdom (Perception) check to discern that the library is animate.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe library makes two attacks.\n\nChained Book\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage, and if the target is a creature, it is grappled (escape 12)."},
  ["creature.animated-coffin.aatm2014"]={title="Animated Coffin",subtitle="Criatura - AATM - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 60 (8d10 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 12 | CON 15 | INT 3 | WIS 11 | CHA 3\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (can't see beyond this radius)\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages of its creator but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nIf the animated coffin is motionless at the start of combat, it has advantage on its initiative roll. Moreover, if a creature hasn't observed the coffin move or act, that creature must succeed on a 18 Intelligence (Investigation) check to discern that the coffin is animate.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe animated coffin can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe animated coffin makes two Slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage.\n\nEntrap\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one Large or smaller creature. hThe target has the grappled condition (escape 13). Until this grapple ends, if the target is not an Undead, the target has the restrained condition and takes 14 (4d6) piercing damage at the start of each of its turns. The animated coffin can grapple only one creature at a time."},
  ["creature.animated-drow-statue.oota2014"]={title="Animated Drow Statue",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 96\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental"},
  ["creature.animated-flying-sword.xmm2024"]={title="Animated Flying Sword",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 17\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 14 (4d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, fly: 50\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 15 | CON 11 | INT 1 | WIS 5 | CHA 1\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlash\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d8 + 2) Slashing damage."},
  ["creature.animated-furniture.coa2014"]={title="Animated Furniture",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 170\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nImunidades: cold, fire, poison, psychic"},
  ["object.animated-ghaunadaur-statue.wdmm2014"]={title="Animated Ghaunadaur Statue",subtitle="Objeto - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 250"},
  ["creature.animated-glass-statue.crcotn2014"]={title="Animated Glass Statue",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 109\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 22 (3d10 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, fly: 60\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 10 | CON 15 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common but can't speak it\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Sight and Smell\n\nThe statue has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight or smell.\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe statue has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the statue's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe statue makes two attacks: one with its beak and one with its talons.\n\nBeak\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (2d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nTalons\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (2d6 + 2) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.animated-halberd.cos2014"]={title="Animated Halberd",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 59\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCA: 15\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nHalberd\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d10 + 1) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.animated-jade-serpent.wdmm2014"]={title="Animated Jade Serpent",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 92\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned"},
  ["creature.animated-knife.egw2014"]={title="Animated Knife",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 248\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: T\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nPV: 12 (5d4)"},
  ["creature.animated-object.xphb2024"]={title="Animated Object",subtitle="Criatura - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 240\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / T/S/M/L/H\n\nCA: 15\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages you know\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nm Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, reach 5 ft. hForce damage equal to 1d4 + 3, 2d6 + 3 + your spellcasting ability modifier (Large), or 2d12 + 3 + your spellcasting ability modifier (Huge)."},
  ["creature.animated-object-huge.phb2014"]={title="Animated Object (Huge)",subtitle="Criatura - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / H\n\nCA: 10\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 6 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAnimated\n\nIf the object lacks legs or other appendages it can use for locomotion, it instead has a flying speed of 30 feet and can hover. If the object is securely attached to a surface or larger object, such as a chain bolted to a wall, its speed is 0.\n\nWhen the animated object drops to 0 hit points, it reverts to its original object form, and any remaining damage carries over to its original object form.\n\nThe DM might rule that a specific objects slam attack inflicts slashing or piercing damage based on its form.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h16 (2d12 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-object-large.phb2014"]={title="Animated Object (Large)",subtitle="Criatura - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCA: 10\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAnimated\n\nIf the object lacks legs or other appendages it can use for locomotion, it instead has a flying speed of 30 feet and can hover. If the object is securely attached to a surface or larger object, such as a chain bolted to a wall, its speed is 0.\n\nWhen the animated object drops to 0 hit points, it reverts to its original object form, and any remaining damage carries over to its original object form.\n\nThe DM might rule that a specific objects slam attack inflicts slashing or piercing damage based on its form.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d10 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-object-medium.phb2014"]={title="Animated Object (Medium)",subtitle="Criatura - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCA: 13\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 12 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAnimated\n\nIf the object lacks legs or other appendages it can use for locomotion, it instead has a flying speed of 30 feet and can hover. If the object is securely attached to a surface or larger object, such as a chain bolted to a wall, its speed is 0.\n\nWhen the animated object drops to 0 hit points, it reverts to its original object form, and any remaining damage carries over to its original object form.\n\nThe DM might rule that a specific objects slam attack inflicts slashing or piercing damage based on its form.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (2d6 + 1) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-object-small.phb2014"]={title="Animated Object (Small)",subtitle="Criatura - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / S\n\nCA: 16\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAnimated\n\nIf the object lacks legs or other appendages it can use for locomotion, it instead has a flying speed of 30 feet and can hover. If the object is securely attached to a surface or larger object, such as a chain bolted to a wall, its speed is 0.\n\nWhen the animated object drops to 0 hit points, it reverts to its original object form, and any remaining damage carries over to its original object form.\n\nThe DM might rule that a specific objects slam attack inflicts slashing or piercing damage based on its form.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-object-tiny.phb2014"]={title="Animated Object (Tiny)",subtitle="Criatura - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / T\n\nCA: 18\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 4 | DEX 18 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAnimated\n\nIf the object lacks legs or other appendages it can use for locomotion, it instead has a flying speed of 30 feet and can hover. If the object is securely attached to a surface or larger object, such as a chain bolted to a wall, its speed is 0.\n\nWhen the animated object drops to 0 hit points, it reverts to its original object form, and any remaining damage carries over to its original object form.\n\nThe DM might rule that a specific objects slam attack inflicts slashing or piercing damage based on its form.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d4 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-rug-of-smothering.xmm2024"]={title="Animated Rug of Smothering",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 17\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 27 (5d10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 1 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSmother\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, the rug can give it the XPHB condition (escape 13) instead of dealing damage. Until the grapple ends, the target has the XPHB and XPHB conditions, is suffocating, and takes 10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage at the start of each of its turns. The rug can smother only one creature at a time.\n\nWhile grappling the target, the rug can't take this action, the rug halves the damage it takes (round down), and the target takes the same amount of damage."},
  ["magicitem.animated-shield.dmg2014"]={title="Animated Shield",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile holding this shield, you can speak its command word as a bonus action to cause it to animate. The shield leaps into the air and hovers in your space to protect you as if you were wielding it, leaving your hands free. The shield remains animated for 1 minute, until you use a bonus action to end this effect, or until you are incapacitated or die, at which point the shield falls to the ground or into your hand if you have one free."},
  ["magicitem.animated-shield.xdmg2024"]={title="Animated Shield",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 229\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile holding this Shield, you can take a XPHB to cause it to animate. The Shield leaps into the air and hovers in your space to protect you as if you were wielding it, leaving your hands free. The Shield remains animate for 1 minute, until you take a XPHB to end this effect, or until you die or have the XPHB condition, at which point the Shield falls to the ground or into your hand if you have one free."},
  ["creature.animated-staff.wdmm2014"]={title="Animated Staff",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 262\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCA: 17\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 12 | CON 10 | INT 18 | WIS 14 | CHA 10\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCharm\n\nA creature can grab the staff out of the air with a successful grapple check against the staff, and grappling the staff does not reduce the creature's speed. Any creature that successfully grapples the staff must succeed on a 12 Charisma saving throw or be charmed by the staff until the staff is no longer in its grasp. While the creature is charmed, the staff can issue commands to it, which the creature does its best to obey. The creature can repeat the saving throw each time it takes damage, ending the effect on itself on a success. A creature that successfully resists the staff's control can't be charmed by it for 24 hours.\n\nA creature holding the staff that isn't charmed by it can use an action to attempt to break the staff over a knee or against a solid surface, doing so with a successful 17 Strength (Athletics) check. Breaking the staff in this manner destroys it.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nStaff of Frost\n\nThe staff has 10 charges. It can expend 1 or more of its charges to cast one of the following spells (save 12): cone of cold (5 charges), fog cloud (1 charge), ice storm (4 charges), or wall of ice (4 charges). It regains 1d6 + 4 expended charges daily at dawn. If the staff expends its last charge, roll a d20. On a 1, the staff turns to water and is destroyed.\n\nMelee Attack\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (2d6) bludgeoning damage plus 1 cold damage."},
  ["creature.animated-statue.wdmm2014"]={title="Animated Statue",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 125\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct"},
  ["creature.animated-statue-of-lolth.wdmm2014"]={title="Animated Statue of Lolth",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 142\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: H\n\nCR: 11\n\nPV: 230 (20d12 + 100)\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal but can't speak"},
  ["creature.animated-stove.wdmm2014"]={title="Animated Stove",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 186\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 50 (50d1)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage.\n\nBelch Fire {@recharge 4}\n\nThe stove belches fire in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the area must make a 10 Dexterity saving throw, taking 22 (4d10) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.animated-table.tftyp2014"]={title="Animated Table",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 230\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 39 (6d10 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 8 | CON 13 | INT 1 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAntimagic Susceptibility\n\nThe table is incapacitated while in the area of an antimagic field. If targeted by dispel magic, the table must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against the caster's spell save DC or fall unconscious for 1 minute.\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the table remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a normal table.\n\nCharge\n\nIf the table moves at least 20 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with a ram attack on the same turn, the target takes an extra 9 (2d8) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nRam\n\nmw 6, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-tile-chimera.rot2014"]={title="Animated Tile Chimera",subtitle="Criatura - RoT - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nResistencias: piercing\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned"},
  ["creature.animated-tree.egw2014"]={title="Animated Tree",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 130\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nIdiomas: understands Common, Druidic, Elvish, and Sylvan but cannot speak"},
  ["creature.animated-wand.wdmm2014"]={title="Animated Wand",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 299\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["feature.animating-performance.tce2014.bard.creation.6"]={title="Animating Performance",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.animatronic-allosaurus.kftgv2014"]={title="Animatronic Allosaurus",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 22\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned"},
  ["creature.ankheg.mm2014"]={title="Ankheg",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14/11\n\nPV: 39 (6d10 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 10\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 11 | CON 13 | INT 1 | WIS 13 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft., tremorsense 60 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) acid damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it is grappled (escape 13). Until this grapple ends, the ankheg can bite only the grappled creature and has advantage on attack rolls to do so.\n\nAcid Spray {@recharge}\n\nThe ankheg spits acid in a line that is 30 feet long and 5 feet wide, provided that it has no creature grappled. Each creature in that line must make a 13 Dexterity saving throw, taking 10 (3d6) acid damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.ankheg.wtthc2014"]={title="Ankheg",subtitle="Criatura - WttHC - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.ankheg.xmm2024"]={title="Ankheg",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 18\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 45 (6d10 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 10\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 11 | CON 14 | INT 1 | WIS 13 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft., Tremorsense 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTunneler\n\nThe ankheg can burrow through solid rock at half its XPHB and leaves a 10-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nm 5 (with XPHB if the target is XPHB by the ankheg), reach 5 ft. h10 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Acid damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 13).\n\nAcid Spray {@recharge}\n\ndex 12, each creature in a 30-foot-long, 5-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 14 (4d6) Acid damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["creature.ankhtepot.rhw2014"]={title="Ankhtepot",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 88\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 202 (27d8 + 81)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 15 | WIS 20 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDarklord Restoration\n\nIf Ankhtepot dies, he revives with all his XPHB in 1d10 weeks somewhere in Har'Akir.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Domain)\n\nIf Ankhtepot fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nAnkhtepot has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAnkhtepot makes four Negative Energy Burst attacks. He can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB.\n\nNegative Energy Burst\n\nm,r 11, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft. h26 (6d6 + 5) Necrotic damage.\n\nTouch of Death {@recharge}\n\nAnkhtepot touches one creature within 5 feet. If the creature has 80 XPHB or fewer, it dies. Otherwise, it takes 52 (8d12) Necrotic damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDeath Strike\n\nAnkhtepot makes one Negative Energy Burst attack.\n\nHand of Fate\n\nstr 19, one Large or smaller creature Ankhtepot can see within 60 feet. actSaveFail 14 (2d8 + 5) Force damage, and the target is pushed or pulled up to 20 feet straight away or toward Ankhtepot. actSaveSuccess Half damage only. actSaveSuccessOrFail Ankhtepot can't take this action again until the start of his next turn.\n\nSands of Time\n\nAnkhtepot teleports up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space he can see. cha 19, each creature in a 10-foot XPHB originating from Ankhtepot at his destination space. actSaveFail 11 (2d10) Necrotic damage, and the target magically ages 10 years. actSaveSuccess Half damage only. actSaveSuccessOrFail Ankhtepot can't take this action again until the start of his next turn."},
  ["creature.ankylosaurus.mm2014"]={title="Ankylosaurus",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 79\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / H\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 68 (8d12 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 11 | CON 15 | INT 2 | WIS 12 | CHA 5\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nTail\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h18 (4d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone."},
  ["creature.ankylosaurus.xmm2024"]={title="Ankylosaurus",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 348\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / H\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 68 (8d12 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 11 | CON 15 | INT 2 | WIS 12 | CHA 5\n\nSalvamentos: \n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe ankylosaurus makes two Tail attacks.\n\nTail\n\nm 6, reach 10 ft. h9 (1d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.ankylosaurus-zombie.toa2014"]={title="Ankylosaurus Zombie",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 240\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / H\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 68 (8d12 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 9 | CON 15 | INT 2 | WIS 6 | CHA 3\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nUndead Fortitude\n\nIf damage reduces the zombie to 0 hit points, it must make a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 5+the damage taken, unless the damage is radiant or from a critical hit. On a success, the zombie drops to 1 hit point instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nTail\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target h18 (4d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone."},
  ["creature.annis-hag.mpmm2014"]={title="Annis Hag",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 47\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 90 (12d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 12 | CON 14 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant, Sylvan\n\nResistencias: cold\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe annis makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (3d6 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (3d6 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nCrushing Hug\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h36 (9d6 + 5) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape 15) if it is a Large or smaller creature. Until the grapple ends, the target takes 36 (9d6 + 5) bludgeoning damage at the start of each of the hag's turns. The hag can't make attacks while grappling a creature in this way."},
  ["creature.annis-hag.vgm2014"]={title="Annis Hag",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 159\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 75 (10d10 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 12 | CON 14 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant, Sylvan\n\nResistencias: cold\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe annis makes three attacks: one with her bite and two with her claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (3d6 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (3d6 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nCrushing Hug\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h36 (9d6 + 5) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape 15) if it is a Large or smaller creature. Until the grapple ends, the target takes 36 (9d6 + 5) bludgeoning damage at the start of each of the hag's turns. The hag can't make attacks while grappling a creature in this way."},
  ["creature.anointed.psa2014"]={title="Anointed",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["spell.antagonize.bmt2014"]={title="Antagonize",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\nYou whisper magical words that antagonize one creature of your choice within range. The target must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the target takes 4d4 psychic damage and must immediately use its reaction to make a melee attack against another creature of your choice that you can see. If the target can't make this attack (for example, because there is no one within its reach or because its reaction is unavailable), the target instead has disadvantage on the next attack roll it makes before the start of your next turn. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage only."},
  ["background.anthropologist.toa2014"]={title="Anthropologist",subtitle="Background - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 191\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Languages:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nCultural Chameleon\n\nBefore becoming an adventurer, you spent much of your adult life away from your homeland, living among people different from your kin. You came to understand these foreign cultures and the ways of their people, who eventually treated you as one of their own. One culture had more of an influence on you than any other, shaping your beliefs and customs. Choose a race whose culture you've adopted, or roll on the Adopted Culture table.\n\nd8 | Culture\n\n1 | Aarakocra\n\n2 | Dwarf\n\n3 | Elf\n\n4 | Goblin\n\n5 | Halfling\n\n6 | Human\n\n7 | Lizardfolk\n\n8 | Orc\n\nFeature: Adept Linguist\n\nYou can communicate with humanoids who don't speak any language you know. You must observe the humanoids interacting with one another for at least 1 day, after which you learn a handful of important words, expressions, and gestures - enough to communicate on a rudimentary level.\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nAnthropologists leave behind the societies into which they were born to discover what life is like in other parts of the world. They seek to see how other races and civilizations survive - or why they did not. Some anthropologists are driven by intellectual curiosity, while others want the fame and recognition that comes with being the first to discover a new people, a lost tribe, or the truth about an ancient empire's downfall.\n\nd6 | Personality Trait\n\n1 | I prefer the company of those who aren't like me, including people of other races\n\n2 | I'm a stickler when it comes to observing proper etiquette and local customs\n\n3 | I would rather observe than meddle\n\n4 | By living among violent people, I have become desensitized to violence.\n\n5 | I would risk life and limb to discover a new culture or unravel the secrets of a dead one.\n\n6 | When I arrive at a new settlement for the first time, I must learn all its customs.\n\nd6 | Ideal\n\n1 | Discovery. I want to be the first person to discover a lost culture. (Any)\n\n2 | Distance. One must not interfere with the affairs of another culture - even one in need of aid. (Lawful)\n\n3 | Knowledge. By understanding other races and cultures, we learn to understand ourselves. (Any)\n\n4 | Power. Common people crave strong leadership, and I do my utmost to provide it. (Lawful)\n\n5 | Protection. I must do everything possible to save a society facing extinction. (Good)\n\n6 | Indifferent. Life is cruel. What's the point in saving people if they're going to die anyway? (Chaotic)\n\nd6 | Bond\n\n1 | My mentor gave me a journal filled with lore and wisdom. Losing it would devastate me.\n\n2 | Having lived among the people of a primeval tribe or clan, I long to return and see how they are faring.\n\n3 | Years ago, tragedy struck the members of an isolated society I befriended, and I will honor them.\n\n4 | I want to learn more about a particular humanoid culture that fascinates me.\n\n5 | I seek to avenge a clan, tribe, kingdom, or empire that was wiped out.\n\n6 | I have a trinket that I believe is the key to finding a long-lost society.\n\nd6 | Flaw\n\n1 | Boats make me seasick.\n\n2 | I talk to myself, and I don't make friends easily.\n\n3 | I believe that I'm intellectually superior to people from other cultures and have much to teach them.\n\n4 | I've picked up some unpleasant habits living among goblins, lizardfolk, or orcs.\n\n5 | I complain about everything.\n\n6 | I wear a tribal mask and never take it off."},
  ["item.antigravity-belt.qftis2014"]={title="Antigravity Belt",subtitle="Item - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\nRaridade: none\n\nMetal tubes ring the lower edge of this wide belt. It is powered by an energy cell stored in a metal case near the buckle. Placing a full energy cell in the belt gives the belt 10 charges.\n\nActivating the Belt\n\nAs a bonus action, you can expend any number of the belt's charges to activate it; the belt remains active for 1 minute per charge expended. You can use a bonus action to deactivate the belt early, but doing so doesn't recover any expended charges.\n\nWhen you activate the belt, and as a bonus action while it remains active, you can rise or descend vertically up to 20 feet. You remain floating in place while the property is active, and you can move yourself horizontally by being pushed or towed or by scooting yourself along a surface, such as a wall or ceiling, at half your walking speed. If you are still levitating when the belt deactivates, you fall.\n\nReplacing the Energy Cell\n\nWhile the belt has charges remaining, its energy cell can't be removed. Once the belt has 0 charges, you can replace the energy cell with a new cell by using an action or a bonus action."},
  ["spell.antilife-shell.phb2014"]={title="Antilife Shell",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\nA shimmering barrier extends out from you in a 10-foot radius and moves with you, remaining centered on you and hedging out creatures other than undead and constructs. The barrier lasts for the duration.\n\nThe barrier prevents an affected creature from passing or reaching through. An affected creature can cast spells or make attacks with ranged or reach weapons through the barrier.\n\nIf you move so that an affected creature is forced to pass through the barrier, the spell ends."},
  ["spell.antilife-shell.xphb2024"]={title="Antilife Shell",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 241\n\nAn aura extends from you in a 10-foot XPHB for the duration. The aura prevents creatures other than Constructs and Undead from passing or reaching through it. An affected creature can cast spells or make attacks with Ranged or Reach weapons through the barrier.\n\nIf you move so that an affected creature is forced to pass through the barrier, the spell ends."},
  ["spell.antimagic-field.phb2014"]={title="Antimagic Field",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\nA 10-foot-radius invisible sphere of antimagic surrounds you. This area is divorced from the magical energy that suffuses the multiverse. Within the sphere, spells can't be cast, summoned creatures disappear, and even magic items become mundane. Until the spell ends, the sphere moves with you, centered on you.\n\nSpells and other magical effects, except those created by an artifact or a deity, are suppressed in the sphere and can't protrude into it. A slot expended to cast a suppressed spell is consumed. While an effect is suppressed, it doesn't function, but the time it spends suppressed counts against its duration.\n\nTargeted Effects\n\nSpells and other magical effects, such as magic missile and charm person, that target a creature or an object in the sphere have no effect on that target.\n\nAreas of Magic\n\nThe area of another spell or magical effect, such as fireball, can't extend into the sphere. If the sphere overlaps an area of magic, the part of the area that is covered by the sphere is suppressed. For example, the flames created by a wall of fire are suppressed within the sphere, creating a gap in the wall if the overlap is large enough.\n\nSpells\n\nAny active spell or other magical effect on a creature or an object in the sphere is suppressed while the creature or object is in it.\n\nMagic Items\n\nThe properties and powers of magic items are suppressed in the sphere. For example, a +1 longsword in the sphere functions as a nonmagical longsword.\n\nA magic weapon's properties and powers are suppressed if it is used against a target in the sphere or wielded by an attacker in the sphere. If a magic weapon or a piece of magic ammunition fully leaves the sphere (for example, if you fire a magic arrow or throw a magic spear at a target outside the sphere), the magic of the item ceases to be suppressed as soon as it exits.\n\nMagical Travel\n\nTeleportation and planar travel fail to work in the sphere, whether the sphere is the destination or the departure point for such magical travel. A portal to another location, world, or plane of existence, as well as an opening to an extradimensional space such as that created by the rope trick spell, temporarily closes while in the sphere.\n\nCreatures and Objects\n\nA creature or object summoned or created by magic temporarily winks out of existence in the sphere. Such a creature instantly reappears once the space the creature occupied is no longer within the sphere.\n\nDispel Magic\n\nSpells and magical effects such as dispel magic have no effect on the sphere. Likewise, the spheres created by different antimagic field spells don't nullify each other."},
  ["spell.antimagic-field.xphb2024"]={title="Antimagic Field",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 241\n\nAn aura of antimagic surrounds you in a 10-foot XPHB. No one can cast spells, take XPHB actions, or create other magical effects inside the aura, and those things can't target or otherwise affect anything inside it. Magical properties of magic items don't work inside the aura or on anything inside it.\n\nAreas of effect created by spells or other magic can't extend into the aura, and no one can teleport into or out of it or use planar travel there. Portals close temporarily while in the aura.\n\nOngoing spells, except those cast by an Artifact or a deity, are suppressed in the area. While an effect is suppressed, it doesn't function, but the time it spends suppressed counts against its duration.\n\nXPHB has no effect on the aura, and the auras created by different XPHB spells don't nullify each other."},
  ["item.antimatter-rifle.dmg2014"]={title="Antimatter Rifle",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 268\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.antimatter-rifle.xdmg2024"]={title="Antimatter Rifle",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 73\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["spell.antipathy-sympathy.phb2014"]={title="Antipathy/Sympathy",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\nThis spell attracts or repels creatures of your choice. You target something within range, either a Huge or smaller object or creature or an area that is no larger than a 200-foot cube. Then specify a kind of intelligent creature, such as red dragons, goblins, or vampires. You invest the target with an aura that either attracts or repels the specified creatures for the duration. Choose antipathy or sympathy as the aura's effect.\n\nAntipathy\n\nThe enchantment causes creatures of the kind you designated to feel an intense urge to leave the area and avoid the target. When such a creature can see the target or comes within 60 feet of it, the creature must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or become frightened. The creature remains frightened while it can see the target or is within 60 feet of it. While frightened by the target, the creature must use its movement to move to the nearest safe spot from which it can't see the target. If the creature moves more than 60 feet from the target and can't see it, the creature is no longer frightened, but the creature becomes frightened again if it regains sight of the target or moves within 60 feet of it.\n\nSympathy\n\nThe enchantment causes the specified creatures to feel an intense urge to approach the target while within 60 feet of it or able to see it. When such a creature can see the target or comes within 60 feet of it, the creature must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or use its movement on each of its turns to enter the area or move within reach of the target. When the creature has done so, it can't willingly move away from the target.\n\nIf the target damages or otherwise harms an affected creature, the affected creature can make a Wisdom saving throw to end the effect, as described below.\n\nEnding the Effect\n\nIf an affected creature ends its turn while not within 60 feet of the target or able to see it, the creature makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a successful save, the creature is no longer affected by the target and recognizes the feeling of repugnance or attraction as magical. In addition, a creature affected by the spell is allowed another Wisdom saving throw every 24 hours while the spell persists.\n\nA creature that successfully saves against this effect is immune to it for 1 minute, after which time it can be affected again."},
  ["spell.antipathy-sympathy.xphb2024"]={title="Antipathy/Sympathy",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 242\n\nAs you cast the spell, choose whether it creates antipathy or sympathy, and target one creature or object that is Huge or smaller. Then specify a kind of creature, such as red dragons, goblins, or vampires. A creature of the chosen kind makes a Wisdom saving throw when it comes within 120 feet of the target. Your choice of antipathy or sympathy determines what happens to a creature when it fails that save:\n\n• Antipathy The creature has the XPHB condition. The XPHB creature must use its movement on its turns to get as far away as possible from the target, moving by the safest route.\n\n• Sympathy The creature has the XPHB condition. The XPHB creature must use its movement on its turns to get as close as possible to the target, moving by the safest route. If the creature is within 5 feet of the target, the creature can't willingly move away. If the target damages the XPHB creature, that creature can make a Wisdom saving throw to end the effect, as described below.\n\nEnding the Effect\n\nIf the XPHB or XPHB creature ends its turn more than 120 feet away from the target, the creature makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a successful save, the creature is no longer affected by the target. A creature that successfully saves against this effect is immune to it for 1 minute, after which it can be affected again."},
  ["item.antitoxin.xphb2024"]={title="Antitoxin",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 222\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAs a XPHB, you can drink a vial of Antitoxin to gain XPHB on saving throws to avoid or end the XPHB condition for 1 hour."},
  ["item.antitoxin-vial.phb2014"]={title="Antitoxin (vial)",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA creature that drinks this vial of liquid gains advantage on saving throws against poison for 1 hour. It confers no benefit to undead or constructs."},
  ["deity.anubis.phb2014"]={title="Anubis",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 299"},
  ["charoption.anvilwrought.mot2014"]={title="Anvilwrought",subtitle="Opcao de Personagem - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 12\n\nYou were forged in the fires of Purphoros's forge. Your appearance bears a metallic sheen and visible joints. The Anvilwrought Characteristics table suggests details of your life or origins. Additionally, you gain the following traits.\n\nConstructed Resilience\n\nYou were created to have remarkable fortitude, represented by the following benefits:\n\n• You have advantage on saving throws against being poisoned, and you have resistance to poison damage.\n\n• You don't need to eat, drink, or breathe.\n\n• You are immune to disease.\n\n• You don't need to sleep, and magic can't put you to sleep.\n\nSentry's Rest\n\nWhen you take a long rest, you must spend at least six hours in an inactive, motionless state, rather than sleeping. In this state, you appear inert, but it doesn't render you unconscious, and you can see and hear as normal.\n\nd6 | Characteristic\n\n1 | An oread who works in Purphoros's forge is the closest thing I have to a parent.\n\n2 | Purphoros made me to serve him.\n\n3 | I was created decades ago and, fearing that I'm growing obsolete, recently fled Mount Velus.\n\n4 | Purphoros regrets my creation and wants to reforge me into something better.\n\n5 | Purphoros intended me to carry on his work by making even greater creations of my own.\n\n6 | Someone in Mount Velus implanted a terrible secret within me in order to smuggle it out into the world."},
  ["creature.anvilwrought-raptor.mot2014"]={title="Anvilwrought Raptor",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 209\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / T\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 18 (4d4 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, fly: 60\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 16 | CON 14 | INT 3 | WIS 14 | CHA 1\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands one language of its creator but can't speak\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Sight\n\nThe raptor has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\nRecorded Mimicry\n\nThe raptor can mimic any sound, including voices, it has heard in the last 24 hours. A creature that hears the sounds can tell they are imitations with a successful 12 Wisdom (Insight) check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe raptor makes two attacks with its beak.\n\nBeak\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.ape.mm2014"]={title="Ape",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 317\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 19 (3d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe ape makes two fist attacks.\n\nFist\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage.\n\nRock\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 25/50 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.ape.xmm2024"]={title="Ape",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 348\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 19 (3d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe ape makes two Fist attacks.\n\nFist\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d4 + 3) Bludgeoning damage.\n\nRock {@recharge}\n\nr 5, range 25/50 ft. h10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."},
  ["deity.apep.phb2014"]={title="Apep",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 299"},
  ["creature.aphemia.mot2014"]={title="Aphemia",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 226\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 52 (8d8 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, fly: 50\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nIf Aphemia fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nAphemia has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAphemia makes two attacks: one with her bite and one with her claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (2d4 + 3) piercing damage plus 13 (3d8) necrotic damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nDiscordant Song\n\nAphemia shrieks a cacophony of magical sounds. Each humanoid within 120 feet of her must succeed on a 14 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened of her until the song ends. A frightened creature takes 7 (2d6) psychic damage at the start of its turn while Aphemia is singing. A frightened creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to Aphemia's Discordant Song for the next 24 hours. Aphemia must take a bonus action on her subsequent turns to continue singing. She can stop singing at any time. The song ends if Aphemia is incapacitated or dies.\n\nGrave Calling Song\n\nAphemia intones a low, growling magical melody. Every undead within 300 feet of her must succeed on a 14 Wisdom saving throw or fall under her control until the song ends. Aphemia must take a bonus action on her subsequent turns to continue singing, and she can mentally command the undead under her control as part of the same bonus action. She can stop singing at any time. The song ends if Aphemia is incapacitated or dies."},
  ["deity.aphrodite.phb2014"]={title="Aphrodite",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 298"},
  ["deity.apollo.phb2014"]={title="Apollo",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 298"},
  ["magicitem.apparatus-of-kwalish.dmg2014"]={title="Apparatus of Kwalish",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis item first appears to be a Large sealed iron barrel weighing 500 pounds. The barrel has a hidden catch, which can be found with a successful 20 Intelligence (Investigation) check. Releasing the catch unlocks a hatch at one end of the barrel, allowing two Medium or smaller creatures to crawl inside. Ten levers are set in a row at the far end, each in a neutral position, able to move either up or down. When certain levers are used, the apparatus transforms to resemble a giant lobster.\n\nThe apparatus of Kwalish is a Large object with the following statistics:\n\n• Armor Class:\n\n• Hit Points:\n\n• Speed:\n\n• Damage Immunities:\n\nTo be used as a vehicle, the apparatus requires one pilot. While the apparatus's hatch is closed, the compartment is airtight and watertight. The compartment holds enough air for 10 hours of breathing, divided by the number of breathing creatures inside.\n\nThe apparatus floats on water. It can also go underwater to a depth of 900 feet. Below that, the vehicle takes 2d6 bludgeoning damage per minute from pressure.\n\nA creature in the compartment can use an action to move as many as two of the apparatus's levers up or down. After each use, a lever goes back to its neutral position. Each lever, from left to right, functions as shown in the Apparatus of Kwalish Levers table.\n\nLever | Up | Down\n\n1 | Legs and tail extend, allowing the apparatus to walk and swim. | Legs and tail retract, reducing the apparatus's speed to 0 and making it unable to benefit from bonuses to speed.\n\n2 | Forward window shutter opens. | Forward window shutter closes.\n\n3 | Side window shutters open (two per side). | Side window shutters close (two per side).\n\n4 | Two claws extend from the front sides of the apparatus. | The claws retract.\n\n5 | Each extended claw makes the following melee weapon attack: 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h 7 (2d6) bludgeoning damage. | Each extended claw makes the following melee weapon attack: 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h The target is grappled (escape 15).\n\n6 | The apparatus walks or swims forward. | The apparatus walks or swims backward.\n\n7 | The apparatus turns 90 degrees left. | The apparatus turns 90 degrees right.\n\n8 | Eyelike fixtures emit bright light in a 30-foot radius and dim light for an additional 30 feet. | The light turns off.\n\n9 | The apparatus sinks as much as 20 feet in liquid. | The apparatus rises up to 20 feet in liquid.\n\n10 | The rear hatch unseals and opens. | The rear hatch closes and seals."},
  ["vehicle.apparatus-of-kwalish.dmg2014"]={title="Apparatus of Kwalish",subtitle="Veiculo - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nThis item first appears to be a Large sealed iron barrel weighing 500 pounds. The barrel has a hidden catch, which can be found with a successful 20 Intelligence (Investigation) check. Releasing the catch unlocks a hatch at one end of the barrel, allowing two Medium or smaller creatures to crawl inside. Ten levers are set in a row at the far end, each in a neutral position, able to move either up or down. When certain levers are used, the apparatus transforms to resemble a giant lobster.\n\nTo be used as a vehicle, the apparatus requires one pilot. While the apparatus's hatch is closed, the compartment is airtight and watertight. The compartment holds enough air for 10 hours of breathing, divided by the number of breathing creatures inside.\n\nThe apparatus floats on water. It can also go underwater to a depth of 900 feet. Below that, the vehicle takes 2d6 bludgeoning damage per minute from pressure.\n\nA creature in the compartment can use an action to move as many as two of the apparatus's levers up or down. After each use, a lever goes back to its neutral position. Each lever, from left to right, functions as shown in the Apparatus of Kwalish Levers table.\n\nLever | Up | Down\n\n1 | Legs and tail extend, allowing the apparatus to walk and swim. | Legs and tail retract, reducing the apparatus's speed to 0 and making it unable to benefit from bonuses to speed.\n\n2 | Forward window shutter opens. | Forward window shutter closes.\n\n3 | Side window shutters open (two per side). | Side window shutters close (two per side).\n\n4 | Two claws extend from the front sides of the apparatus. | The claws retract.\n\n5 | Each extended claw makes the following melee weapon attack: 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h 7 (2d6) bludgeoning damage. | Each extended claw makes the following melee weapon attack: 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h The target is grappled (escape 15).\n\n6 | The apparatus walks or swims forward. | The apparatus walks or swims backward.\n\n7 | The apparatus turns 90 degrees left. | The apparatus turns 90 degrees right.\n\n8 | Eyelike fixtures emit bright light in a 30-foot radius and dim light for an additional 30 feet. | The light turns off.\n\n9 | The apparatus sinks as much as 20 feet in liquid. | The apparatus rises up to 20 feet in liquid.\n\n10 | The rear hatch unseals and opens. | The rear hatch closes and seals."},
  ["magicitem.apparatus-of-kwalish.xdmg2024"]={title="Apparatus of Kwalish",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 229\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis item first appears to be a sealed iron barrel weighing 500 pounds. The barrel has a hidden catch, which can be found with a successful 20 Intelligence (XPHB) check. Releasing the catch unlocks a hatch at one end of the barrel, allowing two Medium or smaller creatures to crawl inside. Ten levers are set in a row at the far end, each in a neutral position, able to move up or down. When certain levers are used, the apparatus transforms to resemble a giant lobster.\n\nThe Apparatus of Kwalish is a Large object with the following statistics: AC 20; HP 200; Speed 30 ft., Swim 30 ft. (or 0 ft. for both if the legs aren't extended); Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage.\n\nTo be used as a vehicle, the apparatus requires one pilot. While the apparatus's hatch is closed, the compartment is airtight and watertight. The compartment holds enough air for 10 hours of breathing, divided by the number of breathing creatures inside.\n\nThe apparatus floats on water. It can also go underwater to a depth of 900 feet. Below that, the vehicle takes 2d6 Bludgeoning damage each minute from pressure.\n\nA creature in the compartment can take a XPHB action to move as many as two of the apparatus's levers up or down. After each use, a lever goes back to its neutral position. Each lever, from left to right, functions as shown in the Apparatus of Kwalish Levers table.\n\nLever | Up | Down\n\n1 | Legs extend, allowing the apparatus to walk and swim. | Legs retract, reducing the apparatus's XPHB and XPHB to 0 and making it unable to benefit from bonuses to speed.\n\n2 | Forward window shutter opens. | Forward window shutter closes.\n\n3 | Side window shutters open (two per side). | Side window shutters close (two per side).\n\n4 | Two claws extend from the front side of the apparatus. | The claws retract.\n\n5 | Each extended claw makes the following melee attack: 8 to hit, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (2d6) Bludgeoning damage. | Each extended claw makes the following melee attack: 8 to hit, reach 5 ft. Hit: The target has the XPHB condition (escape 15).\n\n6 | The apparatus walks or swims forward provided its legs are extended. | The apparatus walks or swims backward provided its legs are extended.\n\n7 | The apparatus turns 90 degrees counterclockwise provided its legs are extended. | The apparatus turns 90 degrees clockwise provided its legs are extended.\n\n8 | Eyelike fixtures emit XPHB in a 30-foot radius and XPHB for an additional 30 feet. | The light turns off.\n\n9 | The apparatus sinks up to 20 feet if it's in liquid. | The apparatus rises up to 20 feet if it's in liquid.\n\n10 | The rear hatch unseals and opens. | The rear hatch closes and seals."},
  ["vehicle.apparatus-of-kwalish.xdmg2024"]={title="Apparatus of Kwalish",subtitle="Veiculo - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 229\n\nThis item first appears to be a sealed iron barrel weighing 500 pounds. The barrel has a hidden catch, which can be found with a successful 20 Intelligence (XPHB) check. Releasing the catch unlocks a hatch at one end of the barrel, allowing two Medium or smaller creatures to crawl inside. Ten levers are set in a row at the far end, each in a neutral position, able to move up or down. When certain levers are used, the apparatus transforms to resemble a giant lobster.\n\nTo be used as a vehicle, the apparatus requires one pilot. While the apparatus's hatch is closed, the compartment is airtight and watertight. The compartment holds enough air for 10 hours of breathing, divided by the number of breathing creatures inside.\n\nThe apparatus floats on water. It can also go underwater to a depth of 900 feet. Below that, the vehicle takes 2d6 Bludgeoning damage each minute from pressure.\n\nA creature in the compartment can take a XPHB action to move as many as two of the apparatus's levers up or down. After each use, a lever goes back to its neutral position. Each lever, from left to right, functions as shown in the Apparatus of Kwalish Levers table.\n\nLever | Up | Down\n\n1 | Legs extend, allowing the apparatus to walk and swim. | Legs retract, reducing the apparatus's XPHB and XPHB to 0 and making it unable to benefit from bonuses to speed.\n\n2 | Forward window shutter opens. | Forward window shutter closes.\n\n3 | Side window shutters open (two per side). | Side window shutters close (two per side).\n\n4 | Two claws extend from the front side of the apparatus. | The claws retract.\n\n5 | Each extended claw makes the following melee attack: 8 to hit, reach 5 ft. h7 (2d6) Bludgeoning damage. | Each extended claw makes the following melee attack: 8 to hit, reach 5 ft. hThe target has the XPHB condition (escape 15).\n\n6 | The apparatus walks or swims forward provided its legs are extended. | The apparatus walks or swims backward provided its legs are extended.\n\n7 | The apparatus turns 90 degrees counterclockwise provided its legs are extended. | The apparatus turns 90 degrees clockwise provided its legs are extended.\n\n8 | Eyelike fixtures emit XPHB in a 30-foot radius and XPHB for an additional 30 feet. | The light turns off.\n\n9 | The apparatus sinks up to 20 feet if it's in liquid. | The apparatus rises up to 20 feet if it's in liquid.\n\n10 | The rear hatch unseals and opens. | The rear hatch closes and seals."},
  ["creature.apprentice.hol2014"]={title="Apprentice",subtitle="Criatura - HoL - 2014",body="Pagina: 201\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 7 (2d8 - 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 10 | CON 9 | INT 13 | WIS 11 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nQuarterstaff\n\nmw 1 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h2 (1d6 - 1) bludgeoning damage, or 3 (1d8 - 1) bludgeoning damage if used with two hands.\n\nBurning Hands (1st-Level Spell; 2/Day)\n\nYou shoot forth a 15-foot cone of fire. Each creature in that area must make a 11 Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes 10 (3d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one The fire ignites any flammable objects in the area that aren't being worn or carried.\n\nFire Bolt (Cantrip)\n\nrs Ranged Spell Attack: 3 to hit, range 120 ft., one target. h5 (1d10) fire damage. A flammable object hit by this spell ignites if it isn't being worn or carried."},
  ["creature.apprentice-wizard.mpmm2014"]={title="Apprentice Wizard",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 259\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 10/13\n\nPV: 13 (3d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 14 | WIS 10 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nArcane Burst\n\nms,rs 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) force damage."},
  ["creature.apprentice-wizard.vgm2014"]={title="Apprentice Wizard",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 209\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 9 (2d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 14 | WIS 10 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h2 (1d4) piercing damage."},
  ["item.aquamarine.dmg2014"]={title="Aquamarine",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA transparent pale blue-green gemstone."},
  ["item.aquamarine.xdmg2024"]={title="Aquamarine",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA pale blue green gemstone."},
  ["feature.aquatic-affinity.xphb2024.druid.sea.6"]={title="Aquatic Affinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 87\n\nThe size of the XPHB created by your Wrath of the Sea increases to 10 feet.\n\nIn addition, you gain a XPHB equal to your XPHB."},
  ["creature.aquatic-ghoul.pota2014"]={title="Aquatic Ghoul",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 87\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30"},
  ["creature.aquatic-troll.rot2014"]={title="Aquatic Troll",subtitle="Criatura - RoT - 2014",body="Pagina: 36\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nResistencias: cold"},
  ["creature.arabelle.cos2014"]={title="Arabelle",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\nPV: 2 (1d8)"},
  ["creature.aradrine-the-owl.crcotn2014"]={title="Aradrine the Owl",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 82\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["deity.araleth-letheranil.mtf2014"]={title="Araleth Letheranil",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43"},
  ["creature.aranea.fraif2014"]={title="Aranea",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 250\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 66 (12d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 17 | CON 12 | INT 12 | WIS 10 | CHA 15\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpider Climb (Hybrid or Spider Form Only)\n\nThe aranea can climb difficult surfaces, including along ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nWeb Walker\n\nThe aranea ignores movement restrictions caused by webs, and it knows the location of any other creature in contact with the same web.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe aranea makes two attacks, using Bite, Slam, or Sling in any combination.\n\nBite (Hybrid or Spider Form Only)\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage plus 2 (1d4) Poison damage.\n\nSlam\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h7 (1d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage.\n\nSling (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nr 5, range 30/120 ft. h8 (2d4 + 3) Bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShape-Shift\n\nThe aranea shape-shifts into a humanoid form, into a humanoid-spider hybrid form, or back into its true spider form. Its game statistics are the same in each form, except where noted. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed."},
  ["creature.arasta.mot2014"]={title="Arasta",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 248\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / H\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 300 (24d12 + 144)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 16 | CON 23 | INT 15 | WIS 22 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Sylvan\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades: acid, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nArmor of Spiders (Mythic Trait; Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nIf Arasta is reduced to 0 hit points, she doesn't die or fall unconscious. Instead, she regains 200 hit points. In addition, Arasta's children immediately swarm over her body to protect her, granting her 100 temporary hit points.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Arasta fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nArasta has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nArasta can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nWeb Walker\n\nArasta ignores movement restrictions caused by webbing.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nArasta makes three attacks: one with her bite and two with her claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h20 (3d8 + 7) piercing damage, and the target must make a 21 Constitution saving throw, taking 32 (5d12) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. If the damage reduces the target to 0 hit points, the target is stable but poisoned for 1 hour, even after regaining hit points, and is paralyzed while poisoned in this way.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (3d6 + 7) slashing damage.\n\nWeb of Hair {@recharge 4}\n\nArasta unleashes her hair in the form of webbing that fills a 30-foot cube next to her. The web is difficult terrain, its area is lightly obscured, and it lasts for 1 minute. Any creature that moves into the web or that starts its turn there must make a 21 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the creature is restrained while in the web. A creature can use an action to make a 21 Strength check. On a success, it can free itself or a creature within 5 feet of it that is restrained by the web. This webbing is immune to all damage except magical fire. A 5-foot cube of the web is destroyed if it takes at least 20 fire damage from a spell or other magical source on a single turn.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaws\n\nArasta makes one attack with her claws.\n\nSwarm (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nArasta causes two swarm of spiders to appear in unoccupied spaces within 5 feet of her.\n\nToxic Web (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nEach creature restrained by Arasta's Web of Hair takes 18 (4d8) poison damage.\n\n=== ACOES MITICAS ===\n\nSwipe\n\nArasta makes two attacks with her claws.\n\nWeb of Hair (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nArasta recharges Web of Hair and uses it.\n\nNyx Weave (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nEach creature restrained by Arasta's Web of Hair must succeed on a 21 Constitution saving throw, or the creature takes 26 (4d12) force damage and any spell of 6th level or lower on it ends."},
  ["deity.arawai.erlw2014"]={title="Arawai",subtitle="Divindade - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 141\n\nArawai is the Sovereign of Life and Love. She is the patron of fertility and of the benevolent aspects of nature, bringing good harvest and gentle rain."},
  ["deity.arawai.phb2014"]={title="Arawai",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 296"},
  ["deity.arawn.phb2014"]={title="Arawn",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 298"},
  ["subclass.arcana-domain.au2014.cleric.arcana.0"]={title="Arcana Domain",subtitle="Subclasse - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Arcana Domain\n\nPagina: 125\n\nMagic is an energy that suffuses the multiverse and that fuels both destruction and creation. Gods of the Arcana domain know the secrets and potential of magic intimately. For some of these gods, magical knowledge is a great responsibility that comes with a special understanding of the nature of reality. Other gods of Arcana see magic as pure power, to be used as its wielder sees fit.\n\nThe gods of this domain are often associated with knowledge, as learning and arcane power tend to go hand-in-hand. In the Realms, deities of this domain include Faerûnian and Faerûnian, as well as Elven of the elven pantheon. In other worlds, this domain includes Greek, Celtic, and Egyptian; the triple moon gods of Dragonlance, Dragonlance, and Dragonlance of Krynn; and Greyhawk, Greyhawk, and Greyhawk of Greyhawk.\n\nAt each indicated cleric level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared. They do not count towards your limit.\n\nCleric Level | Spells\n\n1st | detect magic, magic missile\n\n3rd | magic weapon, Nystul's magic aura\n\n5th | dispel magic, magic circle\n\n7th | arcane eye, Leomund's secret chest\n\n9th | planar binding, teleportation circle\n\nNivel 1 - Arcane Initiate\n\nPagina: 125\n\nWhen you choose this domain at 1st level, you gain proficiency in the Arcana skill, and you gain two cantrips of your choice from the spells. For you, these cantrips count as cleric cantrips.\n\nNivel 1 - Arcane Initiate\n\nNivel 2 - Channel Divinity: Arcane Abjuration\n\nPagina: 125\n\nStarting at 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to abjure otherworldly creatures.\n\nAs an action, you present your holy symbol, and one celestial, elemental, fey, or fiend of your choice that is within 30 feet of you must make a Wisdom saving throw, provided that the creature can see or hear you. If the creature fails its saving throw, it is turned for 1 minute or until it takes any damage.\n\nA turned creature must spend its turns trying to move as far away from you as it can, and it can't willingly end its move in a space within 30 feet of you. It also can't take reactions. For its action, it can use only the Dash action or try to escape from an effect that prevents it from moving. If there's nowhere to move, then the creature can use the Dodge action.\n\nAfter you reach 5th level, when a creature fails its saving throw against your Arcane Abjuration feature, the creature is banished for 1 minute (as in the banishment spell, no concentration required) if it isn't on its plane of origin, and its challenge rating is at or below a certain threshold, as shown below.\n\nCleric level | Banishes Creatures of CR...\n\n5th | 1/2 or lower\n\n8th | 1 or lower\n\n11th | 2 or lower\n\n14th | 3 or lower\n\n17th | 4 or lower\n\nNivel 2 - Channel Divinity: Arcane Abjuration\n\nNivel 3 - Arcana Domain\n\nPagina: 8\n\nAmplify Your Magical Power\n\nMagic suffuses the multiverse and fuels both destruction and creation. Clerics with the Arcana Domain view magical knowledge not as power to be used in pursuit of personal ends, but as a gift they have the responsibility to share.\n\nGods associated with the Arcana Domain know the secrets and potential of magic intimately. These gods are often connected to knowledge, secrecy, or power.\n\nNivel 3 - Arcana Domain\n\nNivel 3 - Arcana Domain Spells\n\nPagina: 8\n\nYour connection to this divine domain means you always have certain spells ready. When you reach a Cleric level specified in the Arcana Domain Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Prepared Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Channel Divinity: Arcane Abjuration\n\nNivel 3 - Fortifying Spell\n\nPagina: 8\n\nOne target of the spell gains a number of XPHB equal to 2d8 plus your Cleric level.\n\nNivel 3 - Fortifying Spell\n\nNivel 3 - Modify Magic\n\nPagina: 8\n\nYou can use your Channel Divinity to alter your spells as you cast them. When you cast a spell, you can expend one use of your Channel Divinity and change the spell in one of the following ways (no action required).\n\nNivel 3 - Student of Arcana\n\nPagina: 8\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nMagical Knowledge\n\nYou gain proficiency in the XPHB skill or one skill of your choice from the skills available to Clerics at level 1.\n\nCantrips\n\nYou learn two spells of your choice. Whenever you gain a Cleric level, you can replace one of these cantrips with another spells.\n\nNivel 3 - Tenacious Spell\n\nPagina: 8\n\nWhen you cast a spell that forces a creature to make a saving throw, and a creature you can see succeeds on that saving throw, roll 1d6 and subtract the number rolled from the target's first saving throw against the spell's effect.\n\nNivel 3 - Tenacious Spell\n\nNivel 6 - Dispelling Recovery\n\nPagina: 9\n\nImmediately after you cast a spell with a spell slot that restores XPHB to a creature or ends a condition on a creature, you can cast XPHB as part of that action, XPHB, or XPHB, and without expending a spell slot.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB or XPHB. You also restore your use of it by expending one use of Channel Divinity (no action required).\n\nNivel 6 - Dispelling Recovery\n\nNivel 6 - Spell Breaker\n\nPagina: 125\n\nStarting at 6th level, when you restore hit points to an ally with a spell of 1st level or higher, you can also end one spell of your choice on that creature. The level of the spell you end must be equal to or lower than the level of the spell slot you use to cast the healing spell.\n\nNivel 8 - Blessed Strikes\n\nPagina: 30\n\n{@i 8th-level cleric tce, which replaces the Potent Spellcasting feature\n\nYou are blessed with divine might in battle. When a creature takes damage from one of your cantrips or weapon attacks, you can also deal 1d8 radiant damage to that creature. Once you deal this damage, you can't use this feature again until the start of your next turn.\n\nNivel 8 - Potent Spellcasting\n\nPagina: 125\n\nStarting at 8th level, you add your Wisdom modifier to the damage you deal with any cleric cantrip.\n\nNivel 17 - Arcane Mastery\n\nPagina: 125\n\nAt 17th level, you choose four spells from the Wizard spell list, one from each of the following levels: 6th, 7th, 8th, and 9th. You add them to your list of domain spells. Like your other domain spells, they are always prepared and count as cleric spells for you.\n\nNivel 17 - Magical Mastery\n\nPagina: 9\n\nYou learn four spells, one from each of levels 6, 7, 8, and 9. You thereafter always have those spells prepared. Whenever you gain a Cleric level, you can replace one of these spells with another spells of the same level."},
  ["feature.arcana-domain.au2014.cleric.arcana.3"]={title="Arcana Domain",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\nAmplify Your Magical Power\n\nMagic suffuses the multiverse and fuels both destruction and creation. Clerics with the Arcana Domain view magical knowledge not as power to be used in pursuit of personal ends, but as a gift they have the responsibility to share.\n\nGods associated with the Arcana Domain know the secrets and potential of magic intimately. These gods are often connected to knowledge, secrecy, or power."},
