ual to 2d8 plus your Cleric level.\n\nNivel 3 - Fortifying Spell\n\nNivel 3 - Modify Magic\n\nPagina: 8\n\nYou can use your Channel Divinity to alter your spells as you cast them. When you cast a spell, you can expend one use of your Channel Divinity and change the spell in one of the following ways (no action required).\n\nNivel 3 - Student of Arcana\n\nPagina: 8\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nMagical Knowledge\n\nYou gain proficiency in the XPHB skill or one skill of your choice from the skills available to Clerics at level 1.\n\nCantrips\n\nYou learn two spells of your choice. Whenever you gain a Cleric level, you can replace one of these cantrips with another spells.\n\nNivel 3 - Tenacious Spell\n\nPagina: 8\n\nWhen you cast a spell that forces a creature to make a saving throw, and a creature you can see succeeds on that saving throw, roll 1d6 and subtract the number rolled from the target's first saving throw against the spell's effect.\n\nNivel 3 - Tenacious Spell\n\nNivel 6 - Dispelling Recovery\n\nPagina: 9\n\nImmediately after you cast a spell with a spell slot that restores XPHB to a creature or ends a condition on a creature, you can cast XPHB as part of that action, XPHB, or XPHB, and without expending a spell slot.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB or XPHB. You also restore your use of it by expending one use of Channel Divinity (no action required).\n\nNivel 6 - Dispelling Recovery\n\nNivel 6 - Spell Breaker\n\nPagina: 125\n\nStarting at 6th level, when you restore hit points to an ally with a spell of 1st level or higher, you can also end one spell of your choice on that creature. The level of the spell you end must be equal to or lower than the level of the spell slot you use to cast the healing spell.\n\nNivel 8 - Blessed Strikes\n\nPagina: 30\n\n{@i 8th-level cleric tce, which replaces the Potent Spellcasting feature\n\nYou are blessed with divine might in battle. When a creature takes damage from